a political maneuver with potentially  far-reaching consequences  Iraq's president has sent his  resignation letter to Parliament saying  he would rather step down than approve a  new prime minister in a three-page  statement Barham Saleh said out of my  kinas to avoid bloodshed and protect  civil peace I will not name Assad ally  Donny as a candidate for the next prime  minister i donnie is the governor of  Basra province he was nominated for the  role by the largest bloc in Parliament  al banna that coalition is made up of  mainly Iranian backed political groups  which is why their candidate is being  fiercely rejected by their opponents  Ayane was picked to replace Adel Abdel  mati who resigned in November after  months of anti-government protests but  the governor has been accused of  neglecting his own province busser is  home to more than 70 percent of Iraq's  oil reserves but locals don't have the  basic necessities like clean water and  reliable electricity I don't think they  will accept his resignation I think they  will try to convince him is that you  must accept our candidate in way or  another but I don't think he will accept  that he will try hard also to push over  in just I say someone who is independent  transparent didn't be inside the  political process and look for the  future of Iraq protesters have strongly  rejected ID on his nomination and that's  the reason President Saleh gave for not  approving the choice it now means since  Mathies resignation no party has  proposed a candidate who has been  acceptable to all sides the protests  which began here in early October have  been about demanding political change in  Iraq and new electoral law was finally  passed on Tuesday which seemed to please  most Iraqis and now this latest move by  president Saleh to reject adonys  candidacy is likely to strengthen the  demonstrators position door such Aparri  al jazeera Baghdad
 

